Aim: To implement the Model–View–Controller (MVC) architecture for managing student records. 
Theory 
MVC splits an application into three connected parts so that data, presentation and control logic can
change independently. 
• Model: stores the student data and the rules for changing it (add, get, delete). 
• View: decides how data is shown to the user (it never changes the data). 
• Controller: receives the user's action, asks the model to update, and selects what the view must
show. 
